{
  "purpose": "Every route the application served at the register's baseline commit, with the one disposition the register records for it — kept, or a redirect to a named successor — so that G2.3's \"every pre-existing route has a verified kept/redirect/gone disposition\" is a list a gate compares rather than a sentence. The list was measured from the baseline commit itself (git ls-tree of src/app at baselineSha), never typed from memory, and scripts/route-gate.ts holds every entry against docs/route-register.json in both directions: an entry the register does not carry, a register disposition that disagrees, a page route marked gone, or a redirect whose successor is not a registered kept route fails the gate. e2e/route-dispositions.spec.ts asserts each disposition over HTTP.",
  "rule": "Brief G2.3: pre-existing user-facing page routes must be kept or redirect with a 308 to a named successor and may never 404 or be gone; gone is available only to API handlers, form endpoints and storage prefixes with no successor, which must return 410 with an explanatory body and carry an ADR. No pre-existing route is gone today, so the gone branch of the gate is enforced and exercised only by its planted test.",
